      "updated": 1763817342383,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's use this to configure our spring\nand load container",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's use this to configure our spring\nand load container",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "R3xfcWZel6i_2_TS8t1uX",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 359.3416878450937,
      "y": 26468.43405098564,
      "width": 834.6452766939775,
      "height": 1750,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bRK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 387346957,
      "version": 159,
      "versionNonce": 1976081251,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763818696285,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "⭐ 1. What does SpringApplication.run() do?\n\nIt:\n\ni)starts the Spring Boot application\n\nii)creates the IoC Container (ApplicationContext)\n\niii)auto-configures beans\n\niv)starts the embedded server (Tomcat)\n\nv)performs component scan\n\nvi)loads application.properties\n\nvii)sets up logging\n\nviii)registers web controllers\n\nix)returns the ApplicationContext\n\nSo this:\n\nApplicationContext context = SpringApplication.run(App.class, args);\n\n\n➡️ Works ONLY in Spring Boot.\n\n⭐ 2. Then how do we create IoC container in Spring Core?\n\nIn Spring Core (non-boot), we manually create the container.\n\n✔ XML-based configuration:\nApplicationContext context =\n        new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext(\"beans.xml\");\n\n✔ Java-based configuration:\n@Configuration\n@ComponentScan(\"com.example\")\npublic class AppConfig {}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        ApplicationContext context =\n                new AnnotationConfigApplicationContext(AppConfig.class);\n\n        Student s = context.getBean(Student.class);\n        s.code();\n    }\n}\n\n\n➡️ Spring Core requires manual container creation.\n\n⭐ 3. Why Spring Boot does NOT require this?\n\nBecause @SpringBootApplication automatically does:\n\n@Configuration\n\n@EnableAutoConfiguration\n\n@ComponentScan\n\nAND\n\nSpringApplication.run() automatically initializes the container.\n\nSo Boot hides the complexity.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "⭐ 1. What does SpringApplication.run() do?\n\nIt:\n\ni)starts the Spring Boot application\n\nii)creates the IoC Container (ApplicationContext)\n\niii)auto-configures beans\n\niv)starts the embedded server (Tomcat)\n\nv)performs component scan\n\nvi)loads application.properties\n\nvii)sets up logging\n\nviii)registers web controllers\n\nix)returns the ApplicationContext\n\nSo this:\n\nApplicationContext context = SpringApplication.run(App.class, args);\n\n\n➡️ Works ONLY in Spring Boot.\n\n⭐ 2. Then how do we create IoC container in Spring Core?\n\nIn Spring Core (non-boot), we manually create the container.\n\n✔ XML-based configuration:\nApplicationContext context =\n        new ClassPathXmlApplicationContext(\"beans.xml\");\n\n✔ Java-based configuration:\n@Configuration\n@ComponentScan(\"com.example\")\npublic class AppConfig {}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        ApplicationContext context =\n                new AnnotationConfigApplicationContext(AppConfig.class);\n\n        Student s = context.getBean(Student.class);\n        s.code();\n    }\n}\n\n\n➡️ Spring Core requires manual container creation.\n\n⭐ 3. Why Spring Boot does NOT require this?\n\nBecause @SpringBootApplication automatically does:\n\n@Configuration\n\n@EnableAutoConfiguration\n\n@ComponentScan\n\nAND\n\nSpringApplication.run() automatically initializes the container.\n\nSo Boot hides the complexity.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
