      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*)Configuring the spring application:in spring boot most of the \nconfiguration we did using annotation like registering bean with\nannotation @Component->Now we can do the same in spring also that's\nwe can use spring annotation @Component but the approach is a bit different",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*)Configuring the spring application:in spring boot most of the \nconfiguration we did using annotation like registering bean with\nannotation @Component->Now we can do the same in spring also that's\nwe can use spring annotation @Component but the approach is a bit different",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VwnCU9kXZNljesUV-e2xe",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 368.53701217410105,
      "y": 28515.43587193643,
      "width": 660,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bRQ",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 441315,
      "version": 84,
      "versionNonce": 444330659,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763818971943,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Spring Based Xml Config :\n\nSpring Framework provides three main methods to create and\nmanage objects within the application context:\n \n1. XML Configuration: Configuring beans using XML files. \n\n2. Java-Based Configuration: Configuring beans using Java\nclasses. \n\n3. Annotations: Configuring beans using annotations directly\nin the code",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Spring Based Xml Config :\n\nSpring Framework provides three main methods to create and manage objects within the application context:\n \n1. XML Configuration: Configuring beans using XML files. \n\n2. Java-Based Configuration: Configuring beans using Java classes. \n\n3. Annotations: Configuring beans using annotations directly in the code",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Uz2ORVfCAnnl-or7-8zwX",
      "type": "image",
      "x": 336.3767726108159,
      "y": 28835.197652933068,
      "width": 856.2921272405805,
      "height": 350.1212953194603,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "transparent",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
