      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What if Constructor Has Multiple Same-Type\nArguments?\n\nExample:\n\npublic Student(Laptop lap1, Laptop lap2) { ...\n}\n\n\nSpring gets confused, so we use:\n\nUsing index:\n<constructor-arg index=\"0\" ref=\"laptop1\"/>\n<constructor-arg index=\"1\" ref=\"laptop2\"/>\n\nUsing name (only if class has parameter names\ncompiled):\n<constructor-arg name=\"lap1\" ref=\"laptop1\"/>\n<constructor-arg name=\"lap2\" ref=\"laptop2\"/>",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What if Constructor Has Multiple Same-Type Arguments?\n\nExample:\n\npublic Student(Laptop lap1, Laptop lap2) { ... }\n\n\nSpring gets confused, so we use:\n\nUsing index:\n<constructor-arg index=\"0\" ref=\"laptop1\"/>\n<constructor-arg index=\"1\" ref=\"laptop2\"/>\n\nUsing name (only if class has parameter names compiled):\n<constructor-arg name=\"lap1\" ref=\"laptop1\"/>\n<constructor-arg name=\"lap2\" ref=\"laptop2\"/>",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
