      "text": "Loose Coupling and Tight Coupling ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Loose Coupling and Tight Coupling ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "B7rVnD3WCdVB9TRmfhDEr",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 594.980060654062,
      "y": 55679.79441331415,
      "width": 1140.2404427382928,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 609100259,
      "version": 214,
      "versionNonce": 525267245,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763880930467,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Loose Coupling vs Tight Coupling (Simple, Clear, Practical Explanation)\n\nThese two concepts explain how much your classes depend on each other.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Loose Coupling vs Tight Coupling (Simple, Clear, Practical Explanation)\n\nThese two concepts explain how much your classes depend on each other.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "OXTATp4RBn2aJh9AbSFgF",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 587.0431173395041,
      "y": 55860.47514261818,
      "width": 920.825410565255,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bTW",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1857509219,
      "version": 178,
      "versionNonce": 97545219,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763880974348,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. What is Tight Coupling? (BAD)\n\nTwo classes are tightly coupled when:\n\n✔ One class directly creates or controls another class\n✔ If class A changes → class B must also change\n✔ Hard to extend\n✔ Hard to test\n✔ Violates OOP principles\n✔ No flexibility\n\n❌ Example: Tight Coupling\nclass Car {\n    void start() {\n        System.out.println(\"Car started\");\n    }\n}\n\nclass Driver {\n    Car car = new Car();  // Driver creates Car (tight coupling)\n\n    void drive() {\n        car.start();\n    }\n}\n\nWhy is this tight coupling?\n\nDriver depends on the concrete class Car\n\nIf you want ElectricCar → You must change Driver class\n\nIf Car constructor changes → You must change Driver\n\n❌ Not extendable\n❌ Not testable\n❌ Not flexible",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. What is Tight Coupling? (BAD)\n\nTwo classes are tightly coupled when:\n\n✔ One class directly creates or controls another class\n✔ If class A changes → class B must also change\n✔ Hard to extend\n✔ Hard to test\n✔ Violates OOP principles\n✔ No flexibility\n\n❌ Example: Tight Coupling\nclass Car {\n    void start() {\n        System.out.println(\"Car started\");\n    }\n}\n\nclass Driver {\n    Car car = new Car();  // Driver creates Car (tight coupling)\n\n    void drive() {\n        car.start();\n    }\n}\n\nWhy is this tight coupling?\n\nDriver depends on the concrete class Car\n\nIf you want ElectricCar → You must change Driver class\n\nIf Car constructor changes → You must change Driver\n\n❌ Not extendable\n❌ Not testable\n❌ Not flexible",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "HSXvkqbJDDb__OwR6r-o3",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 559.1745116232086,
      "y": 56156.021936794634,
      "width": 779.5371685449312,
      "height": 328.3763937019249,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
