    {
      "id": "Ix-6EAT9NCrvJL_kvfqB2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 660.8911178287312,
      "y": 72784.32732046992,
      "width": 899.0028534649293,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bVN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 289685507,
      "version": 106,
      "versionNonce": 610489709,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1763883092158,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "What Is a Primary Bean?\n\nWhen Spring finds multiple beans of the same type, it gets confused during\nautowiring.\n\nExample:\n\n<bean id=\"laptop1\" class=\"org.example.Laptop\"/>\n<bean id=\"laptop2\" class=\"org.example.Laptop\"/>\n\n\nAnd you autowire like:\n\n<bean id=\"student\" class=\"org.example.Student\" autowire=\"byType\" />\n\n\nSpring sees two beans of type Laptop → ❌ Error: NoUniqueBeanDefinitionException\n\nSo how do we tell Spring:\n\n“If there are multiple beans, pick this one by default”?\n\n👉 Using primary bean.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What Is a Primary Bean?\n\nWhen Spring finds multiple beans of the same type, it gets confused during autowiring.\n\nExample:\n\n<bean id=\"laptop1\" class=\"org.example.Laptop\"/>\n<bean id=\"laptop2\" class=\"org.example.Laptop\"/>\n\n\nAnd you autowire like:\n\n<bean id=\"student\" class=\"org.example.Student\" autowire=\"byType\" />\n\n\nSpring sees two beans of type Laptop → ❌ Error: NoUniqueBeanDefinitionException\n\nSo how do we tell Spring:\n\n“If there are multiple beans, pick this one by default”?\n\n👉 Using primary bean.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
